# PROJECT OVERVIEW
Vulcan — browser-based welded joint design tool (AWS D1.1 / AISC 360). React 18 + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind v4 frontend, Pyodide 0.26 runtime, Python engines under `public/python/engines/`. State via Zustand. Phases 1–5 reportedly complete; Phase 6 forensic audit kicked off because input changes (t1, L, etc.) frequently fail to propagate to results.

# ARCHITECTURE
- Frontend: src/ (App.tsx, components/, stores/, lib/, types/)
- Stores: pyodideStore, projectStore, resultsStore, uiStore
- Lib: pyodide.ts (callEngine), fileIO.ts (.vulcan save/load with migration), units.ts
- Python engines (public/python/engines/): classifier, structural (Elastic TWL + IC), fatigue, distortion, metallurgy, process, symbol
- Reference data (public/python/data/): aws_d11_annex_k, aws_d11_table_5_7, aws_d11_table_5_8, aisc_360_j2, electrodes_aws_a5, filler_match, materials_steel/aluminum/stainless
- IPC: callEngine — JS sets input via pyodide.globals, calls Python, retrieves dict result

# CODING PRINCIPLES
Forensic audit doctrine (Phases A–F): assume everything wrong, verify by hand-calc, no fixes until user reviews AUDIT_REPORT.md in Phase G.

# CURRENT STATE
Phase 6 Forensic Audit — Fix batch #1–4 COMPLETE. All 7 Critical findings + C-003 + C-103 fixed (9 fixes total). 7 findings deferred to follow-up PRs (Major UI + Minor cleanup). Regression tests `public/python/tests/test_audit_phase_b.py` — 8/8 pass. `tsc --noEmit` clean. Browser smoke test not yet performed by user.

Fixed: C-001, C-003, C-005, C-007, C-101, C-102, C-103, C-202, C-203.
Deferred (need user direction): C-002, C-004, C-006, C-008, C-104, C-201, C-301.

